@startuml
title Logistics Route Decider — UML Deployment Model
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam wrapWidth 220

node "Dispatcher Workstation" as dispatcher {
  artifact "Dispatcher Web Browser" as web
}

node "Driver Mobile Device" as mobile {
  artifact "Driver Mobile App" as app
}

node "Edge / DMZ" as edge {
  node "API Gateway" as gateway {
    artifact "Gateway Configuration" as gatewaycfg
    artifact "TLS, authentication, rate-limit and routing policies" as policies
  }
}

node "Application Network" as appnet {
  node "Logistics Route Decider Application Node" as appnode {
    node "Java 21 Runtime / Spring Boot 3.x" as jvm {
      artifact "Logistics Route Decider Application" as system {
        component "Dispatch & Management Module" as dispatch
        component "Optimization Engine Module" as optimize
        component "Tracking & Notification Module" as tracking
      }
    }
  }
}

database "Primary Relational Database" as primary {
  artifact "Operational schema: Orders, Batches, Routes, Stops, Drivers, Vehicles, Users" as schema
}

database "Read Replica" as replica {
  artifact "Replicated read-only schema" as readschema
}

cloud "External Mapping / Routing Provider" as mapping {
  artifact "Geocoding, road distance and travel-time API" as mapapi
}

cloud "External Messaging Provider" as messaging {
  artifact "Push / SMS notification API" as notifyapi
}

web --> gateway : HTTPS
app --> gateway : HTTPS
gateway --> system : Protected HTTP / REST
system --> primary : SQL over TLS\nwrite + consistency-sensitive reads
primary --> replica : Asynchronous replication
system --> replica : SQL read-only\nstale-tolerant queries only
optimize --> mapping : HTTPS via RoutingEnginePort
tracking --> messaging : HTTPS via NotificationPort

note right of gateway
Gateway is a separate edge deployment.
It handles transport concerns only;
business rules remain in application modules.
end note

note right of primary
Primary is the sole write authority.
Route optimization and dispatch transactions
must use the primary database.
end note

note bottom of replica
Replica is not writable and may lag.
No automatic failover is implied unless
configured and tested separately.
end note

note bottom of system
Three capability modules run in one deployable
application/runtime. Dispatch invokes Optimization
through an in-process application interface.
No broker or independently deployed microservices
are assumed in this phase.
end note

@enduml